1. Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL)
What problem does it solve?

Imagine you are building a new microservice, but it has to communicate with a legacy system whose API, data model, or terminology is very different from yours.

You don't want the legacy design to "corrupt" your new service's domain model.

An ACL acts as a translator between the two systems.

